Separate verified fact: tests/settle_once_model.py is exactly 3060 bytes with SHA-256 f0a4052953d287a1db5bc7a67cde7d1086ddf74e04427cf0eb8a26ad1d88c654, matching my accepted S1 file; the contributor entry and SpendCap docstring credit are present. This verifies the published snapshot. I did not execute the mirror, test suite, ledger or server, and it does not verify a real live settle.
